        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/a4c791/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-04-28T07:13:35.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I seached the Forums but could not find an answer, hoping someone could help. &nbsp;If a card is in play, such as an environment card like Hostage Situation, or Paparazzi on the Scene, which say \"Hero Cards Cannot Be Played\" or \"Heros Cannot Use Powers\", can you still draw an extra card if you don't perform the other condition. &nbsp;</p><h6>&nbsp;</h6><p>To clarify further, if Hostage Situation is in play and Hero Cards Cannot Be Played, am I able to draw an extra card if I don't use a power on my turn? &nbsp;Both conditions are seemingly met. &nbsp;I have neither played a card (Due to Hostage Situation) nor have I used a power (Due to my own volition), ergo I can draw an extra card.</p><h6>&nbsp;</h6><p>Or do I not get to draw an extra card because the not playing a card portion of this condition was not of my own volition?</p><h6>&nbsp;</h6><p>Thanks</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:41:13.599Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 2,
